        "params": {
          "text": "**SP06: three-tap FIR / moving average**  \n**Predict \u2192 Run \u2192 Inspect \u2192 Break \u2192 Explain.** Run 4 s at 300 Hz; double-click Scope.  \n`y[n]=(x[n]+x[n-1]+x[n-2])/3`, `x[n<0]=0`. Step k samples n=k\u22121 at time k/300 s.  \nPredict: DC stays 0.25 V; 10 Hz gain \u2248 0.98543, phase \u221212\u00b0; 100 Hz cancels.  \nTry: change tap1 factor to 0 and rerun. What happens to the mean and 100 Hz tone?  \n[Open student lab](qrc:/s7studio/help/education/labs/SP06-three-tap-fir/README.md) \u00b7 [MIT convolution lesson](https://sigproc.mit.edu/_static/fall26/lectures/Unit-Sample_Response_and_Convolution-handout.pdf) \u00b7 [MIT block diagrams](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-003-signals-and-systems-fall-2011/resources/mit6_003f11_chap3/) \u00b7 Original S7 exercise, not an official MIT resource.",
          "text_format": "markdown",
          "width": 1770,
          "height": 280,
